IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sca-nouns`

-- State Courts Act 1970 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition -- LAYER 1, PART 1: PRELIMINARY (ss 1 and 2).
-- s 1 (short title) is machinery and has no rule here.  Section 2 is encoded as (a) a table of the ten
-- defined words, each with its kind, what it names, what it points at and the Act's own words (copied
-- from the text by script), and (b) one function for each definition that can be decided from facts.
-- A "no" is given only where the text says no in its own words (a definition that "means"); a word the
-- text says only "includes" is not closed.  See NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING".

§ `Section 2 -- the table of defined words`

-- src:201 | “action” means a civil proceeding commenced by summons or
-- src:202 | in any other manner prescribed by Rules of Court;
@ref s 2 "action" (src:201-202)
`s 2 definition: action` MEANS
    Definition
        WITH term IS "action"
             kind IS Means
             `what the Act names` IS LIST "a civil proceeding commenced by summons", "a civil proceeding commenced in any other manner prescribed by Rules of Court"
             `what the Act points at` IS LIST "Rules of Court"
             `the Act's words` IS "“action” means a civil proceeding commenced by summons or in any other manner prescribed by Rules of Court;"

-- src:204 | “commissioner for oaths” means a commissioner for oaths
-- src:205 | appointed under section 68 of the Supreme Court of
-- src:206 | Judicature Act 1969;
@ref s 2 "commissioner for oaths" (src:204-206)
`s 2 definition: commissioner for oaths` MEANS
    Definition
        WITH term IS "commissioner for oaths"
             kind IS Means
             `what the Act names` IS EMPTY
             `what the Act points at` IS LIST "section 68 of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969"
             `the Act's words` IS "“commissioner for oaths” means a commissioner for oaths appointed under section 68 of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969;"

-- src:208 | “Coroner” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the
-- src:209 | Coroners Act 2010;
@ref s 2 "Coroner" (src:208-209)
`s 2 definition: Coroner` MEANS
    Definition
        WITH term IS "Coroner"
             kind IS `Has the meaning given by another law`
             `what the Act names` IS EMPTY
             `what the Act points at` IS LIST "section 2(1) of the Coroners Act 2010"
             `the Act's words` IS "“Coroner” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Coroners Act 2010;"

-- src:214 | “District Court limit” means $250,000 or any other amount
-- src:215 | specified by an order under section 30;
@ref s 2 "District Court limit" (src:214-215)
`s 2 definition: District Court limit` MEANS
    Definition
        WITH term IS "District Court limit"
             kind IS Means
             `what the Act names` IS LIST "$250,000", "any other amount specified by an order under section 30"
             `what the Act points at` IS LIST "section 30"
             `the Act's words` IS "“District Court limit” means $250,000 or any other amount specified by an order under section 30;"

-- src:217 | “judicial officer” means a District Judge, Magistrate or registrar;
@ref s 2 "judicial officer" (src:217)
`s 2 definition: judicial officer` MEANS
    Definition
        WITH term IS "judicial officer"
             kind IS Means
             `what the Act names` IS LIST "a District Judge", "a Magistrate", "a registrar"
             `what the Act points at` IS EMPTY
             `the Act's words` IS "“judicial officer” means a District Judge, Magistrate or registrar;"

-- src:219 | “Magistrate’s Court limit” means $60,000 or any other amount
-- src:220 | specified by an order under section 52(3);
@ref s 2 "Magistrate's Court limit" (src:219-220)
`s 2 definition: Magistrate's Court limit` MEANS
    Definition
        WITH term IS "Magistrate's Court limit"
             kind IS Means
             `what the Act names` IS LIST "$60,000", "any other amount specified by an order under section 52(3)"
             `what the Act points at` IS LIST "section 52(3)"
             `the Act's words` IS "“Magistrate’s Court limit” means $60,000 or any other amount specified by an order under section 52(3);"

-- src:222 | “prescribed” means prescribed by Rules of Court;
@ref s 2 "prescribed" (src:222)
`s 2 definition: prescribed` MEANS
    Definition
        WITH term IS "prescribed"
             kind IS Means
             `what the Act names` IS LIST "prescribed by Rules of Court"
             `what the Act points at` IS LIST "Rules of Court"
             `the Act's words` IS "“prescribed” means prescribed by Rules of Court;"

-- src:224 | “registrar” means the registrar of the State Courts and includes a
-- src:225 | deputy registrar;
@ref s 2 "registrar" (src:224-225)
`s 2 definition: registrar` MEANS
    Definition
        WITH term IS "registrar"
             kind IS `Means and includes`
             `what the Act names` IS LIST "the registrar of the State Courts", "a deputy registrar"
             `what the Act points at` IS EMPTY
             `the Act's words` IS "“registrar” means the registrar of the State Courts and includes a deputy registrar;"

-- src:227 | “Rules of Court” means Rules of Court made under this Act and
-- src:228 | includes forms;
@ref s 2 "Rules of Court" (src:227-228)
`s 2 definition: Rules of Court` MEANS
    Definition
        WITH term IS "Rules of Court"
             kind IS `Means and includes`
             `what the Act names` IS LIST "Rules of Court made under this Act", "forms"
             `what the Act points at` IS EMPTY
             `the Act's words` IS "“Rules of Court” means Rules of Court made under this Act and includes forms;"

-- src:230 | “seal” includes stamp.
@ref s 2 "seal" (src:230)
`s 2 definition: seal` MEANS
    Definition
        WITH term IS "seal"
             kind IS Includes
             `what the Act names` IS LIST "stamp"
             `what the Act points at` IS EMPTY
             `the Act's words` IS "“seal” includes stamp."

-- The table in the Act's order.
`s 2 the ten definitions` MEANS
    LIST `s 2 definition: action`
       , `s 2 definition: commissioner for oaths`
       , `s 2 definition: Coroner`
       , `s 2 definition: District Court limit`
       , `s 2 definition: judicial officer`
       , `s 2 definition: Magistrate's Court limit`
       , `s 2 definition: prescribed`
       , `s 2 definition: registrar`
       , `s 2 definition: Rules of Court`
       , `s 2 definition: seal`

§ `Section 2 -- the definitions as functions of facts`

-- src:199 | 2. In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires —
@ref s 2 (chapeau) (src:199)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 the definitions in this section apply to this provision` MEANS
    IF `the context otherwise requires`
    THEN -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the context otherwise requires"
         JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:201 | “action” means a civil proceeding commenced by summons or
-- src:202 | in any other manner prescribed by Rules of Court;
@ref s 2 "action" (src:201-202)
GIVEN `it is a civil proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was commenced by summons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was commenced in another manner prescribed by Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 "action" the proceeding is an action` MEANS
    IF `it is a civil proceeding` AND (`it was commenced by summons` OR `it was commenced in another manner prescribed by Rules of Court`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“action” means a civil proceeding commenced by summons or in any other manner prescribed by Rules of Court"
         JUST FALSE

-- src:204 | “commissioner for oaths” means a commissioner for oaths
-- src:205 | appointed under section 68 of the Supreme Court of
-- src:206 | Judicature Act 1969;
@ref s 2 "commissioner for oaths" (src:204-206)
GIVEN `the person was appointed a commissioner for oaths under section 68 of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 "commissioner for oaths" the person is a commissioner for oaths` MEANS
    IF `the person was appointed a commissioner for oaths under section 68 of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“commissioner for oaths” means a commissioner for oaths appointed under section 68"
         JUST FALSE

-- src:208 | “Coroner” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the
-- src:209 | Coroners Act 2010;
@ref s 2 "Coroner" (src:208-209)
GIVEN `the person is a Coroner as section 2(1) of the Coroners Act 2010 gives the word its meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 "Coroner" the person is a Coroner` MEANS
    IF `the person is a Coroner as section 2(1) of the Coroners Act 2010 gives the word its meaning`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Coroner” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Coroners Act 2010" (the meaning is wholly that Act's; the fact is borrowed and asked as an input)
         JUST FALSE

-- src:214 | “District Court limit” means $250,000 or any other amount
-- src:215 | specified by an order under section 30;
@ref s 2 "District Court limit" (src:214-215)
GIVEN `the amount specified by an order under section 30, if there is one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2 "District Court limit" the amount in dollars` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amount specified by an order under section 30, if there is one`
    WHEN JUST amount THEN amount
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 250_000

-- src:217 | “judicial officer” means a District Judge, Magistrate or registrar;
@ref s 2 "judicial officer" (src:217)
GIVEN holder IS A `Holder of an office or post`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 "judicial officer" the holder is a judicial officer` MEANS
    CONSIDER holder
    WHEN `District Judge` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN Magistrate THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Registrar of the State Courts` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- the registrar "includes a deputy registrar" (s 2, "registrar"), so a deputy registrar is a registrar and so a judicial officer
    WHEN `Deputy registrar of the State Courts` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“judicial officer” means a District Judge, Magistrate or registrar"
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:219 | “Magistrate’s Court limit” means $60,000 or any other amount
-- src:220 | specified by an order under section 52(3);
@ref s 2 "Magistrate's Court limit" (src:219-220)
GIVEN `the amount specified by an order under section 52(3), if there is one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2 "Magistrate's Court limit" the amount in dollars` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amount specified by an order under section 52(3), if there is one`
    WHEN JUST amount THEN amount
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 60_000

-- src:222 | “prescribed” means prescribed by Rules of Court;
@ref s 2 "prescribed" (src:222)
GIVEN `it is prescribed by Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 "prescribed" the matter is prescribed` MEANS
    IF `it is prescribed by Rules of Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“prescribed” means prescribed by Rules of Court"
         JUST FALSE

-- src:224 | “registrar” means the registrar of the State Courts and includes a
-- src:225 | deputy registrar;
@ref s 2 "registrar" (src:224-225)
GIVEN holder IS A `Holder of an office or post`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 "registrar" the holder is the registrar` MEANS
    CONSIDER holder
    WHEN `Registrar of the State Courts` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Deputy registrar of the State Courts` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“registrar” means the registrar of the State Courts and includes a deputy registrar"
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:227 | “Rules of Court” means Rules of Court made under this Act and
-- src:228 | includes forms;
@ref s 2 "Rules of Court" (src:227-228)
GIVEN `they were made under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 "Rules of Court" the instrument is within the Rules of Court` MEANS
    IF `they were made under this Act` OR `it is a form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Rules of Court” means Rules of Court made under this Act and includes forms"
         JUST FALSE

-- src:230 | “seal” includes stamp.
@ref s 2 "seal" (src:230)
GIVEN `it is a stamp` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2 "seal" the thing is within the word seal` MEANS
    IF `it is a stamp`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“seal” includes stamp" extends the ordinary meaning of seal and does not close it, so a thing that is not a stamp may still be a seal in the ordinary sense
    ELSE NOTHING
